Algorithm -
1.Start
2.Input N and the N elements.
3.If N is odd, set mid = N/2.
4.If N is even, set mid1 = N/2 - 1 and mid2 = N/2.
5.For each element, count the number of elements smaller than it.
6.For odd N, the element having count = mid is the median.
7.For even N, find the elements having count = mid1 and count = mid2.
8.Calculate their average as the median.
9.Display the median.
10.Stop.


Complexity --->

->Time Complexity: O(N²)
->Outer loop runs N times.
->Inner loop runs N times.
->Therefore, N × N = O(N²).
